Thanks again, Tiago.

I am familiar with your paper, and could conceivably use aerial survey data as independent data regarding animal distributions relative to roads. I will look into it.

Ignoring the road problem for a moment, I would like to delve deeper into the question of resampling from the one long transect. It seems to me that choosing a random start point and resampling every other kilometer along the long transect and considering those 20 'random systematic' 1km sections as independent is not terribly different from doing the same as my initial design.

I apologize if I am beating a dead horse, but I would like to maximize the utility of these data. If they are just not strictly able to be used for larger inference, I don't mind, I will still analyze them to look at temporal trends.

Best wishes,
